 "day-in-the-life.16k.wav": {
  "text": "Day one of my endodontic practice. The chairs are in, the CBCT works, and the website goes live tomorrow. Every specialist website has a referral form. Mine almost did too. Then I asked one question, what happens after a dentist hits submit? With a form, it lands in an inbox. With tooth referral, it lands in a pipeline. So I embedded tooth referral on my website. Referring offices pick a location, attach the x-rays, and send the insurance through a secure patient link. Then I invited the dentists I already know. Now we share the same case, the same messages and the same status. Week four, my analytics show every referral, who sent it and how fast we called. 28 referrals, first contact in under four hours. Starting a practice is hard. Losing referrals shouldn't be part of it.",
